  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitAriansHouse.SiblingsGetAlong": "[pg]You're inclined to agree, it's not often you see siblings getting along like that. Something's been bothering you though... You ask Arian if she regrets changing."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitAriansHouse.SiblingsQuarreling": "[pg]Before you can say anything, you hear the distinct sound of Laika's yell. It seems Boon and Laika are still engaged in a heated argument. Arian winces and immediately apologizes to you."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitAriansHouse.SicklyAndHorny": "[pg]Is he... no, he couldn't be. Arian's still too sickly to get horny... isn't he? You wonder if you should try and spy on him - or maybe listen at the keyhole? Then again, you could just barge on in - if he is playing with himself, maybe he'd like some help?"
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitAriansHouse.SitBesideBed": "[pg]You pull the chair and sit next to [Arian eir] bed."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitAriansHouse.SitSilentlyBeside": "[pg]You simply sit beside [Arian eir] bed."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitAriansHouse.SlightPepVoice": "[pg][say: Come in!] You hear Arian say, detecting a slight pep to [Arian eir] voice. You step inside and smile at Arian as you close the door behind you. [Arian Ey] smiles back at you and motions towards a nearby chair."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitAriansHouse.SorryForShock": "[pg][say: Sorry about that, [name]. I guess I should've been more considerate of the shock it would be to change like this.]"
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitAriansHouse.StammersPlease": "[pg][say: P-please.] Arian stammers, still unable to meet your gaze. You gently tap [Arian em] on the nose and move outside. A short while later you hear [Arian em] yell, [say: C-come in!]"
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitAriansHouse.StillHoveringOver": " and, indeed, still hovering over [Arian eir] "
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitAriansHouse.TakeOfferedChair": "take the offered chair"
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitAriansHouse.TakingAnotherChair": ". Taking another for [Arian em]self. [say: I love when you come visit, [name]. So, what are we going to do today?] [Arian ey] asks, expectantly."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitAriansHouse.TalkAboutTravels": "[pg]You rack your brains; what can you tell him? Finally, you shrug and start talking about your travels in the wilderness beyond Tel'Adre. Seeing how much exploration excites him, you take particular care to detail the many different places you've seen, how hard it is to know what you'll find with the strange [say: shifting] that the demons seem to have caused across the land, and all the many sex-mad monsters you've encountered in your travels."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitAriansHouse.TalkingIsFine": "[pg][say: So, is there anything you'd like to do? Maybe talk?] Arian asks. You reply that talking is fine."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitAriansHouse.ThreatensWithDuster": "[pg][say: You! What did you do to master Arian!?] She threatens you with a duster. Boon rushes in to check on the commotion, drying his wet hands with a piece of cloth. [say: Sis, what's going... on...] He looks at the scene and sighs."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitAriansHouse.TinkeringOccultGear": "The lizan is currently busy tinkering with some occult-looking paraphernalia when you find [Arian em]. You politely cough to attract [Arian eir] attention, then do so again when [Arian ey] fails to heed that. It's only on the third attempt that [Arian ey] looks up apologetically from [Arian eir] work. [say: Ah, [name]; I'm sorry, but I was preoccupied with something.] [Arian ey] states in an apologetic tone, indicating the mess on [Arian eir] desk. [say: Was there something you wanted?] [Arian ey] asks."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitAriansHouse.TwinSlitsWord": "twin sexual slits"
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitAriansHouse.VisitArianConfident": "Figuring that Arian would enjoy your company, you make your way with confidence through the streets leading to the lizan's home. Soon enough, you find yourself standing before the stately home in which [Arian ey] and [Arian eir] ferret associates dwell. You pound heartily on the knocker to announce your presence."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitAriansHouse.VisitSicklyMage": "Deciding to visit the sickly lizan mage, Arian, you promptly start walking. The house is fairly large, at least two stories tall, but it looks pretty ordinary; there's nothing about it to make it really stand out from the other buildings in the neighborhood. It's only the small brass plate on the door that says [say: Arian, Magus] that provides any clue that a wizard lives here. There's a solid brass knocker on the front door, leering and grotesque in shape, so you take hold of the handle and loudly bang it against the door to announce your presence."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitAriansHouse.WaitOnCouch": "However, Arian isn't here right now, so you instead make yourself comfortable on the couch. After a few minutes, Arian [Arian emself] walks in through the entrance. [say: Oh, [name]. I wasn't aware you were here... have you been waiting for long?] [Arian ey] asks. You tell [Arian em] not very long. [say: That's good to hear. So, what can I do for you?] [Arian ey] asks, with a smile."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitAriansHouse.WalkToAriansHouse": "Figuring that Arian would enjoy your company, you make your way with confidence through the streets leading to the lizan's home. Soon enough, you find yourself standing before the stately home in which he and his ferret associates dwell. You pound heartily on the knocker to announce your presence."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitAriansHouse.WhyThankingYou": " ask why he's thanking you."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitAriansHouse.WondersWhatWorking": "[pg]You enter the room, wondering what [Arian ey] might have been working on, but decide it's probably nothing. You note [Arian ey]'s made quite an improvement in health since you first met [Arian em]."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.AcademyDescription": "[pg]Arian smiles. [say: Very well. The academy was a place of study, where mages of all kinds gathered. It was renowned for its extensive library and for being one of the best academies to learn about white magic. It was pretty far from this city, but since the demons attacked I wouldn't expect it to still be standing. Things got pretty ugly before my pupils and I made our escape.]"
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.AcademyOverrun": "[pg]He clears his throat. [say: I had to use my power to help my friends. You see, our academy had been overrun by demons and I tried to fight them. But... of course I was not strong enough to defeat all of them or save everyone. All I could do was protect my pupils and myself.] He coughs, but smiles all the same."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.AgreeToWalkHome": "[pg]You decide that it wouldn't be too much trouble, and tell Arian that you'll give him a hand to get home."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.AidesOverlyWorried": "[pg][say: They are worried about me all the time. Maybe too worried... and it's not like I don't appreciate their concern, but sometimes I feel smothered. Make no mistake, I love them like family, but I like to get out sometimes too.] You give a nod in response, figuring it's what he wants to see."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.ApprenticesAreAides": "[pg]He smiles. [say: You see... my apprentices are actually my aides now. They swore to live their lives in my service as my aides.] So, he's been avoiding his apprentices?"
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.AskAboutApprentices": "[pg]You bring up the last conversation you had with Arian and ask him whatever happened to his apprentices."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.AskHisStory": ", you decide to ask him what his story is."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.AsksAboutAcademy": "[pg]So, he's not originally from Tel'Adre? You suggest he should go into details, tell you about his academy."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.AsksHelpHome": "[pg][say: Could I bother you one more time though?] Arian asks shyly. [say: Would you mind helping me home? My aides are probably pestering the guard to come and find me right about now, and I feel like I got my share of fresh air for the moment.]"
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.AsksHowSo": "[pg]How is that so?"
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.AtHisDoorstep": "[pg]Arian leads you to the doorsteps of his house, and unhooking his arm from around your shoulder he takes your hands in [Arian eir] own and smiles at you. [say: Thank you for the help, and for listening to my story.] Then looking into you eyes expectantly, he asks, [say: Listen [name]. I would love it if you could visit me once in awhile. It can be very lonely here and although my aides are always by my side there are things I simply can't talk about with them. So... could you find time to visit a sickly mage?]"
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.BoredWord": "bored"
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.ConfessesMage": "[pg][say: I'm actually a mage; I've been training in the magical arts ever since I was a kid. If you're wondering about my strange white scales, I have them because I was born with something called albinism, some kind of hereditary disease... I'm not really sure, but that's beside the point. I spent most of my youth inside, stuck at home, studying the white arts. People always said I had a way with magic, some even called me a genius. Some genius, huh? I can't even walk a few blocks without help.] He finishes with a cough, as if for emphasis."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.CoughsThenExplains": "[pg][say: Yes, you are correct my friend. And while I do use my magic in the traditional fashion now, that simply was not an option.] He coughs. [say: But that is a story for another time, I think I've held you enough for now.] He closes his eyes and leans back."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.CouldNotFight": "[pg][say: After saving them, I quickly realized that there was no way we could fight the demons off, so we ran as far and as fast as we could. By the time we made it far enough that I could relax I had already used too much of my magic; and as a result... well... you're looking at it.] He coughs for emphasis."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.CuriousWord": "curious"
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.DemonsInfiltrated": "[pg][say: The demons caught us by surprise--they'd infiltrated the academy and spread their black magic from within. Some of the best and most powerful mages were rendered mindless fucktoys. If I hadn't been in one of the warded practice rooms, I would likely have suffered the same fate.] He falls into a momentary coughing fit as he finishes his sentence. Recollecting himself, he continues, [say: There were so many of them... my pupils were in their room, and by the time I fought my way over, they were on the verge of being taken by a pair of incubi. The black magic left them in no state to fight back, but thankfully I still had the mental capacity to cast, and was able to save them.]"
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.DoAsHeSays": "[pg]You do as he says."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.DoubtsMage": "[pg]You ask if he's really a mage - you thought all the mages in Tel'Adre were kept away from the general populace, projecting the spells that keep the city safe from the demons."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.EnoughForNow": "[pg]You tell him that you've heard enough for this time, so it's probably best if he saves his strength and calls it quits there. [say: Very well. I'll be seeing you then, [name].] He waves you off."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.EscapeIntoDesert": "[pg][say: Anyway, there is not much more to my story. We made our escape and wandered about the desert, until we found Tel'Adre. They were nice enough to take us in and so here we are.] He motions to the area surrounding the two of you."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.ExcuseAndLeave": "[pg]You excuse yourself and head back to camp."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.FeelingPrefix": "[pg]Feeling "
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.HideRealReasons": ", keeping your real reasons for bothering with him to yourself"
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.ImpressiveFeatDoubt": "[pg]You admit that's an impressive feat to pull off... but, can't he just cast magic the usual way? Wouldn't that be better for him, if his technique is so much more draining and physically challenging than the conventional style?"
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.LongStoryBeginning": "[pg]He gives you an apologetic smile. [say: I guess I should start at the beginning; it's a bit of a long story though, so why don't you take a seat?] He motions for you to sit beside him."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.MagicalDemonstration": "[pg][say: So, [name]?] You look at him in response. [say: Can I interest you in a magical demonstration?] You answer in the positive."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.NewMagicMethod": "[pg][say: Ah... Now we're getting to why I'm in such a miserable state. You see I've found a new way to use white magic; one that results in far more powerful spells; problem is it is very unhealthy for the caster.] [Arian Ey] smiles at you weakly. [say: In order to achieve a state of complete concentration, I stop all my bodily functions. My heart stops beating, I stop breathing, I dedicate all of my being to the spell I wish to cast. This is very dangerous, but thanks to this I am able to achieve a degree of concentration that no other mage can.] He gauges your reaction. [say: So what would you say? Impressive? Reckless? Stupid?]"
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.NodToContinue": "[pg]You indicate you understand and he should go on."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.NormalWhiteMagic": "[pg]He holds his hands apart from each other, palm facing palm. [say: Here's what you can normally do with White Magic.] He closes his eyes and focus. You watch as arcs of electrical energy, like a tiny current of lightning, sparkles and crackles from one hand to the next. You comment that's quite a sight"
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.NotInCovenant": "[pg][say: Oh, yes, I really am a mage. But I don't belong to the covenant that protects this town... You see, I'm not fit for the job. And besides that, with my magic... it would kill me...]"
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.NotJustFatigue": " You thought spellcasting merely took fatigue and the proper mindset, not life force, and you express that sentiment to the lizan."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.OverdoneItCough": "[pg][say: I guess I might have overdone it.] He smiles at you goofily, then coughs in what is obviously meant to cover his embarrassment. [say: Thanks for keeping me company, I enjoy our chats a lot, [name]. You've been a great friend for me.] You accept the compliment and tell him that it was nothing"
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.ParkRemovedHouseAdded": "[pg][b:(The park has been removed from Tel'Adre's menu. Arian's house has been added to the homes submenu.)]"
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.PromiseToThink": "[pg]You assure him you'll think about it; it's time he went inside and had some rest. [say: Thank you, I'll be seeing you then.] He releases your hand and slowly walks inside, barely getting the door open before two pairs of arms grab him and drag him in, closing the door behind him. You shrug it off and head back towards camp; that diversion was nice, but you have other things to do."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.RequestContinueStory": "[pg]After you make yourself comfortable, you suggest that he continue his story. He looks at you in surprise at first, but he smiles shortly afterwards. [say: Very well, where was I?] He rubs his chin in thought. [say: Ah, yes.]"
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.SentencePeriod": "."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.SentencePeriodAgain": "."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.ShowsHisTechnique": "[pg][say: Now let me show you what I can do with my technique.] He closes his eyes once more and focuses. His white scales begin glowing as his power increases and you gasp as energy virtually explodes from hand to hand, a cascade of lightning coruscating between his hands with enough fury to consume anything that falls between them. He stops when he racks and begins coughing. Now, that is more impressive, you have to admit to yourself."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.SpotSicklyLizan": "As you enter the ragged remnants of the park, you spot the sickly lizan, Arian, sitting at his usual bench, and greet him. [say: Oh, hello there [name]. Good to see you.] He waves lazily."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.StillListening": "[pg]You show that you're still paying attention and he continues."
  "Scenes.Arianscene.VisitThePark.ThinksItUseless": ", whilst privately thinking to yourself how useless that looks - no wonder they can't fight the demons if this is the best they're capable of"
